# Values this module needs that another plane already owns, pulled at plan/apply time by
# .just/tofu.just:
#
#   <variable>=<repo-relative .sops file>#<sops --extract expression>
#
# References only, never values — that is why this file is committed in the clear while every
# file it names is encrypted. Nothing here keeps a second copy that could drift.

# infra/substitutions/app/backup-location.sops.yaml is the canonical record for both: Velero's
# BackupStorageLocation is a CR whose bucket and region are fixed when Flux renders the manifest,
# so that file has to hold them. This module provisions what they name rather than naming it too.
TF_VAR_backups_bucket=infra/substitutions/app/backup-location.sops.yaml#["stringData"]["B2_BUCKET"]
TF_VAR_region=infra/substitutions/app/backup-location.sops.yaml#["stringData"]["B2_REGION"]
